     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Hello,<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">I have made a minor update, to v0.61.0.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">I added a data table for the &quot;destrieux.scgm&quot; atlas. &quot;plot_brainGraph_gui&quot; now offers the option to show a legend for vertex colors or not. You can also now plot vertex colors based on weighted community membership. &quot;plot_rich_norm&quot; has a new argument, &quot;<a href=\"http://facet.by\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://facet.by&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488249013000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1r3PP_K5TPXcwL0jvCIomM\">facet.by</a>&quot;, that accepts either &quot;density&quot; (the original, default value) or &quot;threshold&quot; (which will work for multi-subject, e.g. DTI data).<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">For specific changes, see on <a href=\"https://github.com/cwatson/brainGraph/commit/d1ccc5bab088f3c84f99c13bbfbe4ea983edc896?short_path=8312ad0#diff-8312ad0561ef661716b48d09478362f3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/cwatson/brainGraph/commit/d1ccc5bab088f3c84f99c13bbfbe4ea983edc896?short_path%3D8312ad0%23diff-8312ad0561ef661716b48d09478362f3&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792488249013000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0vXjkynYUU_9olWGsCoSKj\">Github</a>.<br><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:arial,helvetica,sans-serif\">Chris<br></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
